   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"$TMPDIR/limitless-479-adjudication-hdecgl6u/probe.ts\" F2",
    "output": "{\"totalFailedRuns\":105,\"oldCliWithHeadDaemon\":{\"pages\":[{\"items\":68,\"hasMore\":true}],\"counts\":\"Needs you: 68; PRs awaiting review: 0; Blocked lands: 0\"},\"headCliWithHeadDaemon\":{\"pages\":[{\"items\":68,\"hasMore\":true},{\"items\":37,\"hasMore\":false}],\"counts\":\"Needs you: 105; PRs awaiting review: 0; Blocked lands: 0\"}}"
   },
   "evidence": "The temporary probe extracts the base digest implementation with git show, rewrites only its import paths, and runs it against the head Store through an injected API without network calls. At HEAD, store.ts:697 uses `Math.min(opts.limit ?? MAX_FEED_ITEMS, MAX_FEED_ITEMS)` and line 712 applies the byte limiter. Thus a requested limit of 1000 still produces fewer than 1000 items with hasMore true. The base CLI requests `limit: \"1000\"` but terminates on `if (page.items.length < 1000) break;`, ignoring hasMore. The base Store instead queried with `opts.limit ?? 100`, honoring the requested 1000. Updating the head CLI to understand hasMore does not preserve compatibility for the previous CLI."
  },
